From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the compiler the build was configured with

OptionsIOS6.cmake replaced the C, C++, Objective-C and Objective-C++
compilers with the clang that xcrun finds. That pins the real binary when
CMake was handed the shims in /usr/bin, and it is what a build with Apple's
clang wants. A build configured with another clang, the cross toolchain's
own, had its compilers switched under it instead: CMake saw the Objective-C
compiler change, threw the cache away and configured again for the host.

The compilers are replaced only when the one CMake was given is a /usr/bin
shim.
---
 Source/cmake/OptionsIOS6.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/cmake/OptionsIOS6.cmake b/Source/cmake/OptionsIOS6.cmake
index 3b4345d8b2c14fcae52e419f9bf4efbae67ac6c6..a46e46a9ef4b5a24080ff2eb8a6e32d2198f5d0f 100644
--- a/Source/cmake/OptionsIOS6.cmake
+++ b/Source/cmake/OptionsIOS6.cmake
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ if (_sdk_major_minor AND (NOT CMAKE_OSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET OR CMAKE_OSX_DEPLOYMEN
 endif ()
 
 WEBKIT_XCRUN(_clang -f clang)
-if (EXISTS "${_clang}")
+if (EXISTS "${_clang}" AND CMAKE_C_COMPILER MATCHES "^/usr/bin/")
     set(CMAKE_C_COMPILER "${_clang}")
     set(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER "${_clang}++")
     set(CMAKE_OBJC_COMPILER "${_clang}")
